# /sdd-llm

Purpose:
  Generate or query the LLM-native knowledge layer for SDDRA. Exports
  .sdd/ into machine-readable artifacts (JSON/JSONL/maps/chunks) following
  the llmstxt.org llms.txt standard, and (read-only) reports artifact state.

Owns: commands\sdd-llm.sdd

Usage:
  /sdd-llm
  /sdd-llm --export
  /sdd-llm --pack <key>
  /sdd-llm --query <text>
  /sdd-llm --format md|json

Options:
  --export   (Re)generate .sdd/llm/ from canonical .sdd/
  --pack     Return a minimal context pack for a goal key
  --query    Free-text NL query over the exported corpus
  --format   Output format (md|json, default md)

Mode: READ_ONLY by default; --export performs deterministic generation
(derived artifacts, not source edits).

InitialLoad:
  - .sdd/INDEX.sdd (routing only)
  - .sdd/llm/context-pack.json (if present)
  - .sdd/commands/INDEX.sdd

Rules:
  [LLM-01] /sdd-llm --export MUST be deterministic: same .sdd/ input -> same output.
  [LLM-02] /sdd-llm MUST NOT modify canonical .sdd/ source files.
  [LLM-03] Exported artifacts MUST be marked 'generated - do not hand-edit'.
  [LLM-04] /sdd-llm MUST preserve traceability (file path + section + @refs).

Navigation:
  INDEX: @INDEX.sdd
  LlmLayer: @../llm/README.md
  LlmEntry: @../llm/llms.txt
  ContextPack: @../llm/context-pack.json
  Chunks: @../llm/chunks/

State: +
